Hi Len...

One of the features of the UAE environment is the ability to add
record, device, and driver support to an EPICS environment, without
actually touching the base EPICS distribution.  I have written a very
introductory document on adding device support which you can get at
ftp.gemini.edu://pub/gemini_Central/Controls/EPICS/gscg.bdg.007.dsup.fm
Unfortunately I haven't created the same for record or driver support.

The motor record has all three types of EPICS support, and probably
makes a good demo of how to add it to the UAE environment.  I've put
all the motor stuff into UAE and made it available at
ftp.gemini.edu://pub/staff/goodrich/motorUAE.tar.gz
You should be able to add your capfast databases and source code
into this environment.  What I don't have are any capfast symbols
for the motor record.

Let me know what questions you have.
bret
